  "question": {
    "text": "A man (mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ) and his son (mass <math><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ) are standing on a frictionless surface facing each other. The man pushes his son so that he starts moving at a speed of <math><mn>0.70</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> with respect to the man. The speed of the man with respect to the surface is:",
    "image": null
