  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By conservation of linear momentum,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are initial and final momentum of system (boy + man)</p><p>Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math>......(i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;velocity of boy w.r.t. ground</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;velocity of man w.r.t. ground</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>bm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;velocity of boy w.r.t. man</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>bm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>bm</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;........(ii)</p><p>From equation (i) and (ii),</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>70</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Negative sign shows velocity of man is opposite to boy.</p>",
